index 0000000..b67f0e1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-11-17-state-gc.md
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+# State cleanup implementation plan
+
+**Goal:** Automatically remove old disposable state without losing task, knowledge,
+run history, or evaluation metrics.
+
+**Design:** Add `state.retention_days` (default 30; 0 disables cleanup; range
+0–36500). A filesystem collector handles backups, rejected spool files, hook
+traces, and work/log directories for terminal evaluation batches whose finish
+time is older than the cutoff. Every descendant must also be older than the
+cutoff. Unknown/running batches and batches with running attempts are preserved.
+SQLite, tasks, worktrees, isolation profiles, snapshots and base caches remain.
+
+Use `os.Root` for confinement and skip symbolic links in candidate paths/trees.
+Serialize cleanup using an OS file lock; record the last successful automatic
+cleanup in that file. Invoke after successful spool ingestion, at most daily;
+failures must not prevent ordinary work. Explicit `bint gc` reports errors and
+`--dry-run` lists candidates/bytes without deleting, ingesting or changing the
+cleanup schedule. Scope is the current repository's state only.
+
+**Tech stack:** Existing Go 1.25, SQLite, Cobra and fslock; no new dependencies.
+
+## Implementation
+
+- [x] Write collector tests covering age boundaries, recent descendants, active
+  and unknown batches, symlinks, protected state, dry run, disabled retention,
+  daily scheduling, locking and retry after errors; observe missing-feature failure.
+- [x] Implement `internal/stategc` and config defaults/template/validation.
+- [x] Connect automatic collection to `Workspace.Ingest`; add `bint gc
+  [--dry-run] [--json]` with an app service and CLI integration tests.
+- [x] Document retention scope, manual commands, automatic trigger and disabling.
+- [x] Run affected package tests, full suite, vet and diff checks; review safety
+  and report any verification limits.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Retention of 30 days is an implementation default, pending optional user input.
+- Preserve SQLite history and task/evolution evidence; this change targets
+  disposable files and completed evaluation work/log directories.
+- Work in the supplied clean `bench` checkout; no integration/commit requested.
+- Review fix: terminal evaluation batches can resume concurrently. Hold a SQLite
+  writer reservation through the final eligibility check and filesystem removal,
+  serializing with the runner's status update. Dry runs remain read-only.
+
+## Verification
+
+- New collector, configuration, app integration and CLI end-to-end tests pass,
+  along with CLI/TUI coverage and documentation command checks.
+- Concurrent-resume regression fails when the writer reservation is removed,
+  then passes with it restored.
+- `go vet ./...` passes; Windows cross-check (`GOOS=windows go vet` for
+  stategc/app/cli) passes. Formatting and `git diff --check` pass.
+- `go test ./...` encounters sandbox restrictions on localhost listeners
+  (`socket: operation not permitted`). Observed failing tests:
+  - app: `TestMCPGatewayLogWithDaemon`, `TestMCPGatewayLogOldDaemon404`.
+  - cli: `TestIsoCreateCodexLinkedAndDeadLB`.
+  - eval: `TestCodexProfileLinkedLBArgsBeforeResume`.
+  - iso: `TestHarnessArgs`.
+  - mcpcat/probe: `TestHTTPJSONAndSSE/sse=false`.
+  - mcpgw: `TestSecondDaemonRejected`, `TestInfoFile`, `TestAuthTable`,
+    `TestAdminStopShutsDown`, `TestUpstreamEnv`, `TestUpstreamEnvDefaultsAndMissing`,
+    `TestSecretsScrubbedFromStatus`, `TestReviewerDoesNotSeeWriteTools`,
+    `TestDeniedCallsNeverReachUpstream`, `TestRoleResolutionFailsClosed`,
+    `TestInteractiveIsProjectScoped`, `TestToolsCacheSurvivesDaemonRestart`,
+    `TestExclusiveGroup`, `TestGroupMaxConcurrent`, `TestHTTPUpstreamSharedHandshake`.
+  Packages that panic stop before their remaining tests, so this is not a
+  complete green suite. No production data was collected during verification.
+- The workflow package reached the suite's cumulative 10-minute timeout while
+  `TestSessionCompleteStepOverMaxCostRecordsError` was running (for 3 seconds).
+  That test passes on its own (`-count=1 -timeout=60s`, 2.465 seconds).
